#implementation

- implement a token parser for human.skills
- implementation is in typescript
- [path][line] numbers are targets and get updated after coding.
- $Linter, $GoToDefinition and $Highlighter work on *.bot as well as *.human

# version control
- version: 0.3.0
- update for all modules
  - vscode/package.json
  - package.json

#vscode deployment
- package as a .vsix, installed with code --install-extension
- bundle the server and client with esbuild into vscode/dist
- the server runs on the node that comes with vscode
- publisher is benjit87
- published to the marketplace
- provide a bash script to install locally

# npm package for cli
- package for pushing to npm repository
- provide a bash script for it npm.sh

@Data
- *.human file
- *.bot file

@Structure
- each child line starts with exactly one bullet marker
- nest a child by adding 2 spaces before its bullet marker for each level
- never show nesting by repeating bullet markers on the same line
- indent using spaces only; any other indentation is an error
- a line with only an operator after its bullet marker lists that operator
- both *.bot and *.human have the same structure

@Token
- @
- $
- ?
- //
- #
- ->
- +
- word // can represent methods or a defined behavior or just a sentence, semantically driven
- comment_sentence // the words after // , this represent instructions or remarks
- ==
- -
- word // a // inside quotes e.g "//" is a word, not a comment
- % // attach to the name, e.g %tokenize, no space

@Node
- @Token // the token of this line
- children // @Node list, defined by - bullets and indent

@Tokens
- @Token // list

?Data
- @Data

?Parsed
- AST of @Node // tree of nodes, one per line

$Parser
- provide relevant method signatures
- @Data -> tokenize -> @Tokens
- @Tokens + @Structure -> parser -> ?Parsed

$GoToDefinition
- provide relevant method signatures with some explaination
- single .human file plus its sibling *.bot only
- on a definition header of @,$,?,# go to the same header in the *.bot
- for % in *.bot it means go to the code file and line
- if no *.bot or header, stay on the definition

$Highlighter
- provide relevant method signatures with some explaination
- each token type gets its own color
- @Token -> colour -> editor
- @
- $
- ?
- #
- "//"
- ->
- +
- ==
- -
- %

$Linter
- provide relevant method signatures with some explaination
- unused-definition is a warning
- missing-robot only checked when file info is passed
- [path][line] target must exist, warning if the file or line is missing
- [path] is relative to the folder that holds .git or the parent of spec folder
- missing-human, same as missing-robot, for *.bot

$LSP
- $GoToDefinition
- $Linter

$Skill
- source is the SKILL.md that ships inside the onlyhuman library, fixed in the library, not looked up from the user path
- copy as is, no generating or editing
- nothing from the user repo is used
- target is .onlyhuman/SKILL.md under the user path

$CLI
- cli def supports both name form and position form
- $GoToDefinition
- $Linter
- $Skill
